export anchor CinemascopeStyle:
    number: 356
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Cinemascope
    idea: The editor framed as a widescreen film, with solid black letterbox bars carrying opening titles and the export, a 2.39 to 1 picture, and the bin and inspector set below as centred end credits with dotted leaders.
    base: dark
    palette:
        letterbox: #000000, the top and bottom bars and the picture itself
        auditorium: #0e0c0a, the warm dark between the bars and the style sheet
        seat: #16130f, swatch and control cells
        rule: #3a3226, hairline rules framing the timeline
        leader: #5c5243, dotted credit leaders and the render line
        ivory: #efe6d2, text, the playhead and focus
        parchment: #a89e8a, small caps labels and italic asides
        clip: #8a7b5c, clip bars and outlined buttons
        marqueeGold: #d9b56a, the title, section caps, the selected clip, marker and Export
    type:
        Display is a Didone stack, Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Hoefler
        Text, Georgia. Body is a book serif stack, Iowan Old Style,
        Palatino, Georgia, 15px at 1.6. Labels are system sans in caps,
        widely tracked. The title Launch teaser is 44px caps tracked 0.32em
        in gold, the picture card Didone italic up to 38px, the timecode
        serif italic 18px, credit heads sans 13px caps tracked 0.42em,
        credit roles serif italic and credit values sans 13px tracked
        0.14em.
    layout:
        The page is a film. A solid black top bar centres Brightwork Cut in
        tracked caps with an italic presents, then the gold title, then
        1080p and 24 fps in tracked caps. Between the bars a warm near black
        stage holds a centred picture at 2.39 to 1 on black with a faint
        gold spill beneath, the timecode set like an italic subtitle with of
        and the duration, and three bare transport glyphs with play inside a
        thin gold ring. Below, The Timeline is centred in tracked gold caps
        with an italic aside, and the tracks run as hairline rows. Clips are
        thin 4px bars with italic names sitting above them, the selected
        title bar gold, ringed, and followed by a star and the word
        selected. A gold triangle marker with an italic cut to logo and a
        dotted drop line sits at 84 seconds, and an ivory playhead with an
        up triangle and 18. Then two centred credit columns, Featuring the
        bin with file names and durations joined by dotted leaders, and
        Title card with Position 960 by 540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100
        percent and Cross dissolve 12 frames the same way. A solid black
        bottom bar holds a hairline render line with Render 0% and not yet
        begun beside a gold Export in tracked caps. At phone width the bars
        shrink, the credits hide and the track names reduce to their ids.
    spacing: Generous. 40px letterbox bars, 56px between acts, 64px between credit columns.
    density: Low. One wide picture, one thin timeline, two short credit lists.
    corners: None anywhere except the round play ring.
    borders: Hairline rules and dotted leaders only.
    shadows: A faint gold spill below the picture, as if from a projector.
    icons: Very few. Filled transport glyphs, a triangle for the marker, a star for the selection. No icon boxes.
    focus: A 2px ivory outline offset 3px.
    tone: Cinematic and courteous, such as presents, Featuring and not yet begun.
